      "narrative": "Little Giant, Okanogan-Wenatchee NF, USFS. CIMT (NW Team 12). CIMT is also managing the Sisi incident. Thirty miles northwest of Leavenworth, WA. Timber and dormant brush. Minimal fire behavior with creeping, backing and smoldering. Structures threatened. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Sisi, Okanogan-Wenatchee NF, USFS. Ten miles northwest of Stehekin, WA. Closed timber litter and timber. Moderate fire behavior with backing, creeping and flanking. Residences threatened. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Austin, Mt. Hood NF, USFS. Transfer of command from CIMT (CA Team 2) back to the local unit will occur today. CIMT is also managing the Grasshopper and The Narrows incidents. Twenty-five miles southeast of Estacada, OR. Brush, timber and closed timber litter. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering and creeping. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Reduction in acreage due to more accurate mapping. Grasshopper, Mt. Hood NF, USFS. Fourteen miles southwest of Dufur, OR. Brush, hardwood litter and closed timber litter. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering and creeping. Area, road and trail closures in effect. The Narrows, Mt. Hood NF, USFS. Fifteen miles southeast of Estacada, OR. Grass, brush and light slash. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering. Last report unless significant activity occurs. Sinlahekin, Northeast Region, Washington DNR. One mile west of Tonasket, WA. Timber, brush and grass. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering and creeping. Area, road and trail closures in effect. Hagen, Umatilla NF, USFS. Twenty-six miles east of Pendleton, OR. Timber. Minimal fire behavior with smoldering. Last report unless significant activity occurs. Three Queens, Okanogan-Wenatchee NF, USFS. Six miles east of Snoqualmie Pass, WA. Timber, brush and grass. No new information. Last narrative report unless new information is received."
